Duke
Card 01 shows Duke, the Java mascot. Sun Microsystems open sourced Duke on 13 November 2006 under the New BSD license
(https://wiki.openjdk.org/display/duke/Main, https://github.com/openjdk/duke). The picture on our card is a redrawn
version of the official Duke artwork. The Duke project asks everyone to treat Duke with the same respect that Sun and
Oracle have. Java and Duke are trademarks of Oracle and its affiliates.

AI generated pictures
All pictures were generated with ChatGPT image generation from prompts written by Johannes Rabauer, then placed into
card layouts drawn by a script. Whether and how copyright applies to AI generated images is not settled. CC BY 4.0
covers whatever rights exist in the pictures. It gives no guarantee that any rights exist.

Names and characters
The cards are named after Java projects, tools and concepts. The characters are original inventions that play with the
idea of each name. They are not the official logos or mascots (except Duke), and this project is not affiliated with,
sponsored by or endorsed by the owners of those names. All names and trademarks belong to their owners.

Stats
Startup, Clean and Community are opinions made up for game balance. They are not measurements.
